Tier: T4
Why: Sends device pushes to locked screens from a shared outbox with consent, quiet hours and token cleanup; a fault leaks private detail, ignores a mute, or sends to a dead or reassigned device.
T4 trigger scan: lock-screen copy at send, push tokens (DeviceNotRegistered cleanup), consent at send time, multi-replica claim/lease concurrency, inbox visibility of stored notifications.
T3 trigger scan: booking lifecycle emitters, drip, purchase and payout notice writers.
Bounded T1: NO.
Canonical builder: T4 builder lane B-PUSH2-120 (agent 120 wave).
Parent owner: operator (agent 120 wave).
Acceptance evidence: test/push-delivery-round5.spec.ts (15 cases), Sol P2 probe 7/7, Opus U1/U4 and live L1-L6 on Postgres at 53796f1e (ci-lane run 37352088482); every required PR check green at the exact head; Opus and Sol verdicts at the exact head.
Promotion triggers: already T4. Any change to the claim SQL, consent checks, token handling or lock-screen copy needs fresh dual exact-head verdicts.

